  "observed": "The row exists from startup, before any prompt, with the -s id. pid is the process the Terminal runs and pid_start its field 22. `/new` adds a second row for the same pid and pid_start and keeps the first until the process ends, so two rows match. In default mode no leader process runs; with --leader the row still names the Terminal's process while a child `grok-linux-aarch64 agent leader` holds the session's events.jsonl. Rows go when the process ends."
